WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.010
The internet is a great place to find out
all the facts about your favorite celebrities—unless,

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.629
of course, that celebrity is Chuck Norris.

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:12.090
For Norris fans, the internet is a minefield
of lies, jokes, and memes.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:16.860
"When the boogie man goes to sleep every night,
he checks his closet for Chuck Norris."

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.640
So how do you sort the real from the fake?

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:25.720
Keep watching to learn some things you didn’t
know about Chuck Norris.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:26.720
Military man

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.340
Chuck Norris is a famous guy for playing badass
military men, but that isn't all Hollywood

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.520
movie magic.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.680
In fact, Norris did actually serve in the
military, joining the Air Force at the age

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.680
of 18.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.930
His four-year stint proved to be life-changing.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:44.070
While serving at the Osan Air Base in South
Korea, Norris took his first martial arts

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.350
lessons, in Tang Soo Do.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:49.090
The rest, like so many of Chuck's big-screen
bad guys, is history.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:54.620
(gun shots)

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.649
Carlos Norris

00:00:56.649 --> 00:01:00.130
Norris has played a lot of roles over the
course of his career, but one role you may

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:03.420
not be familiar with is Carlos Norris.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.079
In his autobiography, Against All Odds: My
Story, Norris revealed that he got the nickname

00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:12.909
of "Chuck" while serving in the Air Force
in South Korea, but he was born with the name

00:01:12.909 --> 00:01:15.670
Carlos, in honor of his dad's minister.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.470
It doesn't quite have the same ring, does
it?

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:19.691
"Poor Carlos"

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.480
On the other hand, his brother Wieland was
named after a beer...so maybe Chuck got off

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:25.920
easy.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:31.639
(insane Bruce Lee punching)

00:01:31.639 --> 00:01:33.569
Brotherly Dedication

00:01:33.569 --> 00:01:38.130
Norris' most famous film role is Colonel James
Braddock, the former prisoner of war who returns

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:42.570
to Vietnam to save his captive comrades in
Missing in Action and its sequels.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:46.189
That story was very personal for Norris, as
his younger brother Wieland Norris was killed

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:48.409
in Vietnam in 1970.

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:50.270
Chuck later wrote that Wieland met his end

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:53.069
"...while leading his squad through dangerous
enemy territory.

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:57.990
He had spotted an enemy patrol laying a trap
and was trying to warn his men when the Vietcong

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:58.990
cut him down."

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:03.079
Norris dedicated Missing in Action to his
brother's memory.

00:02:03.079 --> 00:02:04.389
Karate World Champ

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:08.319
Following his honorable discharge from the
military, Norris opened a karate school in

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:12.120
the US and started participating in national
competitions.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.250
People might forget now, but he started as
a legitimate karate master.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:21.120
By the end of the 1960s, he had risen to become
the middleweight professional karate champion

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.459
of the world.

00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:26.080
He caught the attention of stars like Bruce
Lee and Steve McQueen, who encouraged him

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.900
to go into acting.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.989
Norris was inducted into the International
Karate &amp; Kickboxing Hall of Fame-

00:02:30.989 --> 00:02:34.589
"YYYAAAAA!!"

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.580
-and in his own words, he became

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:42.380
"The first man ever in the Western Hemisphere
to be awarded an 8th degree Black Belt Grand

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:48.860
Master recognition in the Tae Kwon Do system….something
that still humbles me to the core of my being."

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.900
Saturday Morning Superhero

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.421
By the mid-'80s, Norris had become a household
name, so he parlayed that notoriety into his

00:02:55.421 --> 00:02:57.709
own cartoon and comic books.

00:02:57.709 --> 00:03:03.000
Chuck Norris: Karate Kommandos premiered in
1986 and tanked only after five episodes.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.599
"Chuck Norris, with his team, Pepper!"

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:07.340
"It's too dangerous Chuck!"

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.340
"Too much!"

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.340
"Too much!"

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.799
"Kimo the Samurai warrior!"

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:13.939
"Reed, Chuck's teenage apprentice!"

00:03:13.939 --> 00:03:17.920
But that was still enough for Marvel Comics
to put out an adaptation of the series.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.739
The comic focused more on Chuck himself, which
unfortunately wasn’t a recipe for success,

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:23.739
either.

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:25.989
The publisher pulled the plug after just four
issues.

00:03:25.989 --> 00:03:27.670
And the action figures?

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.719
"Chuck Norris Karate Kommandos"

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:34.239
(theme song)

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.400
"Figures sold seperately"

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.360
Not worth much today.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:38.650
What was wrong with kids in the '80s?

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.939
Speedboat Racer

00:03:39.939 --> 00:03:45.189
When he’s not saving the world and avenging
evil, Chuck Norris has another passion: racing

00:03:45.189 --> 00:03:46.319
speedboats.

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:50.700
In the late '80s, Norris got into the high-powered
and highly dangerous sport alongside fellow

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.709
action stars Kurt Russell and Don Johnson.

00:03:53.709 --> 00:03:55.760
Why did he enjoy racing speedboats?

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.760
He told People,

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.530
"I do it for kicks.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.749
And right now I'm looking forward to kicking
some butt."

00:04:01.749 --> 00:04:02.749
Campaign Trail

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.840
"My plan to secure the border?

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.609
Two words.

00:04:07.609 --> 00:04:08.609
Chuck Norris."

00:04:08.609 --> 00:04:14.019
In 2007, Norris began a new role as a blogger
and political activist, appearing alongside

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:17.500
Republican presidential candidate Mike Huckabee
at major events.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:22.290
It didn't actually help Huckabee win anything,
but that hasn't deterred Norris, who continued

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:25.560
to campaign for Huckabee during the subsequent
presidential election cycle.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:32.070
"Now one of the Chuck Norris facts is that
America's not a democracy, it's a Chucktatorship."

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:33.070
Thanks for watching!

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:36.000
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.820
And leave us a comment to let us know what
you’ve heard about Chuck Norris…

